From 640b72ee5adefdcb319e5c9d1a9b517b741d1917 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 09:14:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add Db8Predictor: a DictionaryPredictor backed by webOS
 db8

Same idea as DictionaryPredictor - prefix-match tokens out of a word
list - except the word list lives in webOS's db8 rather than a flat
file. A standing db8 subscription (luna://com.palm.db/find,
subscribe:true) keeps an in-memory copy of the current word list up
to date; predict() only ever reads that copy, so a keystroke never
waits on the bus, and a restore that repopulates db8 (which always
ends in a reboot on this platform) is picked up automatically the
next time this predictor is constructed - no separate file to
regenerate.

Configured the same way DictionaryPredictor is, with KIND (a db8
kind name) in place of DICTIONARY (a file path) and the same
PROBABILITY.

luna-service2 and json-c are only ever available (and only ever
needed) for the target build - this recipe also builds a native
variant for build-time tools like text2ngram, which must keep
configuring and building without them, so detection is non-fatal
and Db8Predictor drops out of the build entirely (USE_DB8PREDICTOR)
if either is missing, the same way USE_SQLITE already does for
optional SQLite support.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [webOS-ports specific]
